# Auditor sync-count probe — G5 (7E), candidate 9f90e4f
# Date: 2026-11-07
# Purpose: prove the actual hipStreamSynchronize count on a warm layer.

## Source finding
src/kernels/attention.hip:
  struct LayerGuard { DeviceLayerWorkspace& ws;
      ~LayerGuard() { try { ws.drain(); } catch (...) {} } };
  -> the destructor runs on NORMAL return, not only on exception.
  drain(): hipStreamSynchronize(compute_stream); hipStreamSynchronize(copy_stream)
  normal path also: hipStreamSynchronize(ws.copy_stream) at the D2H boundary.
  => 3 syncs per warm layer call.
  print_layer_trace prints a hardcoded "boundary_syncs=1"; it is not a counter.

